Items dropped close together are hard to pick: the labels pile up on top of each other, a click often hits the wrong item, and 10 sticks take 10 clicks. With this mod each pile has one label, and the number on it is what you get with one click. The same works for nearby mushrooms, herbs, and other things that you gather in a moment.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Merged labels.[/b] Items of the same kind within 2 m share one label with the total, such as "Stick (11)". Ready mushrooms and herbs merge too.[/*]
[*][b]One click for the whole pile.[/b] Click a label to pick up everything on it. With the labels off, a click also takes the same items within 2 m.[/*]
[*][b]One click for nearby mushrooms and herbs.[/b] Click "Dandelions (5)" to gather all 5 at once. This works for ready mushrooms, herbs, sticks, small stones, and Clay Deposits.[/*]
[*][b]Clay, mud, and sand in one action.[/b] Collect clay, mud, or sand by hand, and one action also takes the same ground within 1 m.[/*]
[*][b]Take one with a middle-click.[/b] Middle-click a label to take only one. Hold the middle mouse button to turn the camera as before.[/*]
[*][b]No overlapping labels.[/b] Labels move up or down until each has its own space. Action hints such as "LMB Pick up" move to a panel above the hotbar.[/*]
[*][b]Fair play.[/b] Everything gives its normal yield, XP, and cost, and your bag limits apply. A whole pile takes the time of one pickup.[/*]
[*][b]Save safety.[/b] The mod writes nothing to your save, so you can remove it at any time. Made for single player: co-op is not tested.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Last Plague: Blight 0.12.7 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx for The Last Plague: Blight[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\BepInEx\plugins\ProximityPickup.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]ProximityPickup.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.thelastplagueblight.proximitypickup.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-proximity-pickup/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

